CM_ "2023 Jeep Renegade (FCA small-wide / SUSW platform). EPS/ABS/ENGINE/LKAS definitions carried over from fca_giorgio.dbc and chrysler_cusw.dbc where the FCA CRC-8 validates on this car; CRUISE_BUTTONS, ACC_STATUS_1/2 decoded from raw CAN C captures (see docs/susw-dbc-notes.md).";
CM_ BO_ 259 "Raw CAN C only, 100 Hz. ACC_ENGAGED tracks stock ACC engage/resume and cancel (button or brake) exactly.";
CM_ BO_ 348 "Raw CAN C only, 10 Hz while ACC is disengaged and 50 Hz while engaged. ACC_ENGAGED duplicates ACC_STATUS_1.";
CM_ BO_ 502 "CH. Camera to EPS. 4 bytes on this platform (CUSW layout), not Giorgio's 8.";
CM_ SG_ 502 LKAS_CONTROL_BIT "1 = camera has lanes and is armed to intervene (cluster car icon green); 99.8 % agreement with LKA_HUD_2 lanes-detected state on route 000000d8. Not torque-active: only 9 % of set frames carry torque. Flickers faster than the icon (runs down to 0.16 s) - cluster debounces.";
CM_ BO_ 762 "Raw CAN C only, 50 Hz, from BCM (SCCM_CRS_CTRL). 4 bytes; byte 1 = counter (low nibble) + DISTANCE_INC (bit7); byte 3 always 0. CHECKSUM = FCA CRC-8 (poly 0x1D, init 0xFF, xor 0xFF) over bytes 0-1. Bit map differs from CUSW.";
CM_ SG_ 762 ACC_DISTANCE_DEC "gap decrease button (byte0 bit6)";
CM_ SG_ 762 ACC_DISTANCE_INC "gap increase button (byte1 bit7)";
CM_ SG_ 762 ACC_SET_DECEL "SET when not engaged, speed - when engaged";
CM_ SG_ 762 ACC_ACCEL "RES+ / speed + when engaged";
CM_ SG_ 259 ACC_SUBSTATE "1 was observed only while ACC_ENGAGED; it resets after some disengagements, including eight falling edges after ACC_ENGAGED cleared. Meaning TBD.";
CM_ SG_ 257 MAYBE_ACC_BRAKE "may correlate with ACC-actuated braking";
CM_ BO_ 1351 "CH, 4 Hz, camera HUD status. byte6 drives the cluster car icon: 0x02 grey (on, no lanes), 0x0c green (lanes detected, active), 0x14/0x10 yellow intervention (0x14 coincides with positive LKAS_COMMAND torque, 0x10 with the opposite side), 0xcc seen at departure warnings in route 00000003.";
CM_ SG_ 1351 LANESENSE_DISABLED "toggled with the LaneSense button in route 00000003; 0 for all of route 000000ca where LaneSense was on throughout";
CM_ SG_ 1351 WARN_BYTE0 "0 or 6, only during departure warnings";
CM_ SG_ 1351 WARN_BYTE1 "0/64/128 toggling fast during departure warnings (chime/haptic pattern?)";
CM_ SG_ 1351 WARN_BYTE5 "0 or 64, only during departure warnings";
CM_ SG_ 900 LANESENSE_BUTTON "1 while the LaneSense button is held; confirmed on route 000000d8 (8 presses incl. two 10 s holds), each followed by LKA_HUD_2.LANESENSE_DISABLED toggling";
CM_ SG_ 900 UNKNOWN_BYTE2_BITS_1_3 "Former lead-vehicle candidate; 159 transitions and poor edge specificity in route 000000d8. No semantic assignment.";
CM_ BO_ 1852 "Raw CAN C only. Sent at 1 Hz and immediately on change. Cluster ACC display. bytes 0-2 constant (0x00 0x9f 0xc0).";
CM_ SG_ 1852 ACC_SET_SPEED_MPH "0 when no set speed; 34..40, 28..40 etc. match the narrated set speeds press for press";
CM_ SG_ 1852 ACC_POPUP "5-second cluster popup code: 14 ACC on, 15 set/engaged, 17 cancelled, 13 seen before ACC enabled; 0 otherwise";
CM_ SG_ 1852 ACC_GAP_LEAD_BITS "byte6 bits 0-5: steps +/-1 with gap inc/dec while engaged (range seen 6-9, four gap settings) but also changes with lead-vehicle detected/lost; field split TBD";
CM_ SG_ 1852 ACC_HUD_POPUP_2 "byte6 bits 6-7 set for ~5 s after ACC events";
CM_ SG_ 1852 ACC_STATE "0 off, 1 on/ready (after ACC on button, no set speed), 2 engaged, 5 standby after cancel (set speed retained), 3 and 4 one-frame transitions (cancel, engage)";
CM_ BO_ 1850 "Raw CAN C only, 1 Hz. byte0 = hour, byte1 = minute, BCD, local time";
CM_ BO_ 1444 "Raw CAN C only, 1 Hz. byte1 bits 4/5 remain a provisional blind-spot hypothesis: 80 transitions aligned with positive narration windows and none in the negative-control window. Isolated left/right captures are still required. The noisier 0x770 hypothesis was rejected.";
CM_ SG_ 1351 LKA_HUD_STATE "byte6 bits 0-5, enumerated (bit-field readings do not fit all values): 2 grey car (LaneSense on, no lanes), 12 green (lanes acquired, armed), 16 yellow left departure (negative LKAS torque), 20 yellow right departure (positive torque), 12 also held during the hands-off warning (0xcc); 8/22/24/0 seen rarely, unmapped";
CM_ SG_ 1351 LKA_WARNING_BITS "byte6 bits 6-7: 3 during the captured combined lane-departure + hands-off warning (0xcc with green state, 0xd0 with yellow-left); 0 otherwise. Hands-off-only behavior was not captured.";
VAL_ 1351 LKA_HUD_STATE 2 "GREY_NO_LANES" 12 "GREEN_ARMED" 16 "YELLOW_LEFT" 20 "YELLOW_RIGHT" ;
